    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d134">

                <pb facs="0156" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/2800</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-12-27T16:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                                1917, 4 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 28, 11.31
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2141. Following message signed “Robins”<anchor n="1" xml:id="d134-f1"/> for committee on Red
                    Cross: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>December 26. State Department’s 1920, December 21.<anchor n="2"
                                xml:id="d134-f2"/> Please urge upon the President the necessity of
                            our continued intercourse with Bolshevik government. Otherwise
                            impossible to arrange for transportation and distribution of supplies,
                            particularly milk. Ambassador approves this statement and has advised
                            State Department to the same effect. Alleged statement of Trotsky, quoted in your message, untrue.
                            Statement made by me to Trotsky
                            was from your cables regarding shipment of supplies.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Please note my approval as stated above.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Francis</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d134-f1" n="1" xml:id="d134-f1-content">
                <p>Lieut. Col. Raymond Robins, in charge of
                    the American Red Cross Commission to Russia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d134-f2" n="2" xml:id="d134-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; cf. Department’s telegrams No. 1883, Dec. 6, and No. 1917, Dec. 20,
                    and the Ambassador’s telegram No. 2091, Dec. 11, <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_289">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>,
                        pp. 289</ref>, <ref target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_319">319</ref>, and <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_301">301</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
